{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011396-why-life-is-strange-is-false-premise-on-wisdom","id":1011396,"title":"Why Life is Strange is false premise on Wisdom","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-03T00:04:09-08:00","id":1011396,"title":"Why Life is Strange is false premise on Wisdom","content":"It\u2019s topic about <a href=\"http://www.ign.com/games/life-is-strange/pc-20022934\" target=\"_blank\">video game</a> that is one of best depiction of Acanthus Path and their powers. Discussion will be based on spoilers, cause you cannot talk about it without talking the plot of game. If you did not play it, go play. <i>Right</i> now. No, really, go <b>right now</b>. It will change your life. We will wait\u2026<br /> <br /> Okay, you played? To the end? Great! Now we can talk about Awakened Wisdom and this game. So Max is archetypical Acanthus \u2013 she is photographer, she can rewind time, she has visions and sense Destiny over her. And at the start of the game she saves her long-not-seen best friend Chloe. From them, she saves her\u2026 a lot. And here we comes to how this game is wrong in eyes of Awakened.<br /> <br /> On start, Max have a vision with Lighthouse and great hurricane. Lighthouse can be obvious read as Lunargent Watchtower, especially as she gets her rewind power after this. Problem is with the storm. In final it\u2019s uncovered it\u2019s gigantic Paradox-like event she created with her time manipulations. Manipulations that started with saving Chloe and most of time were about rescuing her. So game say to save town from the hurricane, she must let Chloe die in their first encounter. Which any Acanthus will say is bul@#%it!<br /> <br /> If games was right, that meant you get your time rewind powers to save your friend \u2013 only to use them to <i>not save</i> her in the first place! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It\u2019s totally illogical and inappropriate. It\u2019s the worst story ending also \u2013 much better would even that Max is running to the Chloe attacker and dies trying to save her. Or even most probably in <b>Mage</b> would be that Max jumps in to hurricane, finds Abyssal Demon running it and make a bargain.<br /> <br /> Sacrificing your loved one from the powers that let you saved her in first place must some Exarchs plot, surely!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-03-2016, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T01:38:59-08:00","id":1011410,"title":"","content":"Seems right for me. You used your powers for selfish reasons without seeing the bigger picture over and over again, then got burned. Learn your lessons, understand that one life is nothing in the grand scheme of things. There are no free meals, either be selfish and sacrifice tons of people for your own desire or be wise and let one life end to save endless others.<br /> <br /> Then again, Max is less of a Mage and more of a unfortunate Proximi. I also was incredibly confused after finishing the game and reading that people thought that saving Chole was supposed to be &quot;good&quot; ending and were dissapointed by how it was handled. Like, what? People really think that selfish decision to save one person in face of a city-wrecking catastrophe should be praised and framed as a great thing to do???<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Anyway, it's also perfectly Acanthus-y in the way that it's all about seeing different consequences play out and seeing how much YOU can change. YOU have the power. YOU can decide the outcome. You are RESPONSIBLE for the choice you made. No matter what ending you pick, it's your and only your fault. If Chole died, it's your fault. If city died, it's your fault. There are no easy choices. If you can live with being a mass-murderer, go and save her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 12-03-2016, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T02:27:31-08:00","id":1011425,"title":"","content":"You have the power to see and change the Consequences of your Choices.<br /> <br /> Know that you, and only you, are responsible for your Choice, made by your own free will, and its Consequences.<br /> <br /> Yep, seems Acanthus to me. Remember, none of the Path's perspective on the world do not always coincide with human notions of morality. Neither is Wisdom. &quot;But of course, Saving The Girl is the only moral and right choice it could be!&quot; is a deeply human sentiment. A human gifted with time powers will likely come to that conclusion, no matter how many 'unimportant' 'background' lives they have to sacrifice. Because you are the Hero of the Story, who gets the Princess at the end, right?<br /> <br /> The Acanthus laugh at such destinies. The road to hell is paved with good intentions, and to Witches and Enchanters, to be Wise is to foresee what Consequences your Choices brings to the world at large. If the only way to stop the predestined Bad Ending is to kill the childhood friend, or trusted comrade, or the princess, or the mentor, or whatever... then so be it.<br /> <br /> But then again, some Acanthus say &quot;Screw that&quot; to even that, and will save one friend over millions of innocent lives anyway because why the hell not. And they are perfectly and clearly aware of how much blood they are getting on their hands.<br /> <br /> And people still say mages aren't monstrous. (That last one's not directed at you, wyrd. Just an overall frustration.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T02:30:33-08:00","id":1011426,"title":"","content":"The thing is - hurricane was prophesied by her! It means that whatever she would done, storm would still hit the town. It's really not her consequences - it's some outsider force fucking with whole Arcadia Bay, plain and simple. ( Or in <b>Mage</b> term - Exarchs being bitch. )<br /> <br /> More, Max COULD easily save all town, even when saving Chloe! With strange occurrences by the <i>whole week</i> - snow on start of October, eclipse, mass numbers of whales on the beach, FREAKING DOUBLE MOON - that I would point as interesting markings of Paradox for <b>Mage</b>, I may add - it's weird she just cannot tale people night before storm 'Run for you lives, this coming hurricane will kill you all!'<br /> <br /> Even if wondering how she would predicated it all, seeing how this all weird weather patterns collide in one last week. And how Max saved Kate before, 'being in right place' - Would made most people to wonder and go on one or two day trip to distant families. Just to be sure.<br /> <br /> This binary ending is bullshit, as with this kind of story - you are lead straight to the thesis ending ( hurricane you saw in your own vision ). Or Storyteller do not let you take actions that are logical in this environment ( alerting town in advance ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T02:33:18-08:00","id":1011427,"title":"","content":"Love is an Exarch trap, designed to deceive you and distract you from truly Wise matters. It encourages selfishness and lulls you to satisfaction in chains of Lie. It tricks you into thinking that temporal and fleeting relationship is worth more than anything else, blinding you to the whole world. It also will, ultimately, lead into greater despair sooner or later. <br /> Tricking you into thinking that your &quot;loved one&quot; is anything special or more important than others is Exarchs victory, and seeing past that is road to Wisdom.<br /> <br /> (I'm little facetious here, but yeah, &quot;saving the girl damn the consequences&quot; is poster-child for UnWise Selfish Mage Dickery)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T02:35:41-08:00","id":1011429,"title":"","content":"You could easily translate the plot into Mage by making it a Mystery that connects Chole's Destiny directly to the fate of town, where avoiding fulfilling the former will make Fate go &quot;blarp&quot; and resolve itself by doing the Hurricane. No need for Exarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T02:41:54-08:00","id":1011430,"title":"","content":"It's like 'we must save town from hurricane I had vision with' -&gt; 'okay, let's use your time powers that let you see this hurricane' -&gt; 'we made hurricane by stoping hurricane' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What kind of moral it is? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> 'Do nothing, as when you do what we serving you, you will destroy the world'?<br /> <br /> I say it loudly - it must be Exarchs plot, plain and simple. As it's illogical to summon disaster by trying to prevent it with powers showing you disaster in the first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-03-2016, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T02:48:55-08:00","id":1011432,"title":"","content":"Yeah, events in Life in Strange don't clearly fall into &quot;It's an Awakening&quot;, &quot;No it's a Joining&quot;, &quot;It is Wise&quot;, &quot;No it's Unwise&quot; categories.<br /> <br /> We'll just have to dissect it into little packets of abstract concepts about metaphysical lessons, so that we can internalize it enough to use it for playing Mage games. Just like what mages do to mysteries for juicy Arcane Beats <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, and if this was an indeed Arcadian Awakening... let's just remember that things like Time and causality are often described as malleable at best in such phenomena. Especially when prophecies get involved, Greek mythology style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 12-03-2016, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T02:55:59-08:00","id":1011433,"title":"","content":"Not talking about a Mage, for a moment?<br /> The moral in the game is that there are things beyond your control, things that you cannot change. It's about accepting that while some things can be slowed, they can't be stopped. It's about valuing friendship and understanding that your loved ones could be gone any minute, right now, so you should be happy for the time you had with them and never take them as granted.<br /> It's about letting go after they are gone, and soldiering forward, instead of living in the past.<br /> <br /> In the end, this game isn't about changing the past, it's about coming to terms with loss. Time travel *isn't framed as a good thing* here. It isn't a cool superpower. Trying to change the past only bring disaster and unhappiness. &quot;But you can go back and save the town simply by...!&quot; is kinda missing the point. <br /> <br /> These are, by the way, very common tropes. Time travel is a literary device used exactly to impart these lessons very, very often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T03:04:29-08:00","id":1011436,"title":"","content":"You could interpret it as Max just not having the knowlegde she needs. She's not part of an Order, things like paradox are not explained to her.<br /> <br /> I see it as her sometimes absorbing paradox into her pattern, causing headaches and nosebleeds (and nightmare visions near the end).<br /> But mostly she releases the paradox, getting a bunch of manifestations and twisting of fate. The hurricane came from that.<br /> <br /> If this was a Mage game.<br /> As it is, the ending was allright. She could have spent more time tweaking ways to save Chloe from getting shot, but it would take away from the impact of having to choose to let the town be destroyed and countless people die, and choosing to let Chloe die knowing she could stop it.<br /> <br /> It the same choice she made with William (Chloe's dad). She stood by and let him die, because a future where he lives is unacceptable to her. No matter how tragic it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11799,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","user":"RBAWintrow","date":".  Misspelled her as het every single time. 12-03-2016, 06:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T03:09:43-08:00","id":1011439,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I sympathized way more with William and David (!) than with Chole. While my opinions here would be the same no matter who she was, I never liked her. It would just make me little more sadder to kill her, instead of being all like &quot;finally!!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T03:43:45-08:00","id":1011443,"title":"","content":"I agree with the thesis &quot;Max is a Proximus&quot;: she had only one/two power from Time Arcana. And the inferior Arcanum of Acanthus is Force: th Hurricane could be an effect of a upgraded curse.<br /> I dont agree with WHW about time traveling as device for show &quot;moral faillure&quot;: the idea that human cannot bear more possibility and control about own choise is a Lie , very Exarchesque.<br /> We all gather knowledge from our mistake and petty fail: and overcome theme with new ability acquired / refined with hard work.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T04:10:50-08:00","id":1011450,"title":"","content":"You have perfect control about your choice. You can kill thousands to make one life or kill one to safe thousands. Acanthus is cursed and blessed at the same time, as they get to make this choice. <br /> Then again note that when talking about moral and using time travel as device I was talking abuot the game in general, not in context of Mage the Awakening. Obviously, this show won't perfectly translate to Mage, mostly because it's not Mage and it was written with different stances and ideas in mind (for example, indeed for an Acanthus time travel is a tool to make their choices, while in game it represents unability to cope with events too hard to swallow). <br /> <br /> Again, honestly, any of these ending choices can be Wise or Unwise. The key to Wisdom here is not what you choose, but seeing the bigger picture; did you decide to become a mass murderer willingly, taking full responsibility for your actions and with perfect understanding of what will it lead to?<br /> You are Wise.<br /> <br /> Did you do it on impulse, to save a girl, without thinking it through?<br /> You are Unwise.<br /> <br /> Wisdom is not about picking the morally right option, or good option, or comfortable option. It's about understanding consequences, reasons and interconnections, especially when looking at it through Acanthus Arcana. Your choice being informed is more important than the choice itself as far as Wisdom is concerned. That's why doing something labeled as unwise is not automatically a Wisdom loss; it's just harder and harder to understand and keep track of it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T05:16:51-08:00","id":1011458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011396-why-life-is-strange-is-false-premise-on-wisdom?p=1011450#post1011450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wisdom is not about picking the morally right option, or good option, or comfortable option. It's about understanding consequences, reasons and interconnections, especially when looking at it through Acanthus Arcana. Your choice being informed is more important than the choice itself as far as Wisdom is concerned. That's why doing something labeled as unwise is not automatically a Wisdom loss; it's just harder and harder to understand and keep track of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the planned murder is much more okay than manslaughter for the Wisdom, yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T05:48:35-08:00","id":1011464,"title":"","content":"Yes. Premeditated Murder is Wisdom 4-7 Sin, Manslaughter is Wisdom 1-3 Sin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T12:17:43-08:00","id":1011612,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I feel that Fate magic would gain a lot if it had a similar concept of Kharmic Debt, where when you manipulate luck using your powers, luck has to *come from somewhere*; every lucky break you arrange for yourself is luck stolen from someone else. Current Fate is just...all upside, no downsides, free meals, just lucky breaks, no consequences unless you homebrew some. It's more wish fulfillment than personal horror/dark urban fantasy.<br /> So yeah, I would be totally for some kind of energy build up that accompanies heavy Fate magic (kind of like fucking around with Forces should unshape local weather patterns, Mind will traumatize people, and so on), with Arcadian Tornado being a neat example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T12:27:45-08:00","id":1011615,"title":"","content":"Was this meant to be in a different thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T12:36:47-08:00","id":1011618,"title":"","content":"Your powers having a terrible price isn't really one of Mage's themes, though. The idea that having control over Fate (and using said control) having innate negative consequences is something the setting seems to deliberately <i>not</i> have (or at least doesn't state up-front). The bad stuff that comes from monkeying with Fate and the horrible chains of unintended side-effects aren't because the gods decided to fuck you; they are <i>your </i>fault, absolutely and decidedly. If it's just an automatic thing that happens no matter what, it removes the whole idea of trying to balance Wisdom with action and instead makes it a question of total abstinence for any sane person or reckless abandon for everyone else.<br /> <br /> Mage gives you a really shiny, pretty rope and goodness, look at that, you've made it into a noose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T12:59:33-08:00","id":1011623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011396-why-life-is-strange-is-false-premise-on-wisdom?p=1011618#post1011618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bad stuff that comes from monkeying with Fate and the horrible chains of unintended side-effects aren't because the gods decided to fuck you; they are <i>your </i>fault, absolutely and decidedly. If it's just an automatic thing that happens no matter what, it removes the whole idea of trying to balance Wisdom with action and instead makes it a question of total abstinence for any sane person or reckless abandon for everyone else.<br /> <br /> Mage gives you a really shiny, pretty rope and goodness, look at that, you've made it into a noose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why <b>Life is Strange</b> works only on <i>seemingly</i> notice when comparing to Mage - Hurricane is foretold by yourself so it's not really your own consequences, it was premeditate orchestrated this way.<br /> <br /> Or Silver Ladder are totally right and Wisdom <i>is</i> artificially created moral code entwine in universe by Exarchs to punish all opposition on to what <i>could</i> be done with Supernal Magic on world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T13:43:16-08:00","id":1011644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011396-why-life-is-strange-is-false-premise-on-wisdom?p=1011623#post1011623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why <b>Life is Strange</b> works only on <i>seemingly</i> notice when comparing to Mage</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, it isn't Mage. Any time you draw parallels to another piece of media, there will be parts that work and parts that don't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011396-why-life-is-strange-is-false-premise-on-wisdom?p=1011623#post1011623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> - Hurricane is foretold by yourself so it's not really your own consequences, it was premeditate orchestrated this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Max saw the storm in a vision, but she didn't know that using her time travel abilities would be what caused it until near the end of the game. Really, the thing that makes it un-Magelike isn't the fact that she had a vision of it (future vision is a pretty standard Time power), it's that the storm seems to be more of a cosmic karma thing, like Chloe was &quot;supposed&quot; to die, and saving her created this kind of karmic backlash of fate that would kill thousands more. But, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> observed, that's not really how Fate works in Awakening. There <i>is</i> a way to interpret it that fits better into Mage, but it's still not perfect, and honestly I doubt you'll like it anyway as you seem to have strongly disliked the ending of the game.<br /> <br /> Think about it this way. When Max awakened, she saw the watchtower. (the lighthouse) As an Acanthus, her Astral Journey took her through time, showing her a glimpse of a possible future, though at the time she couldn't quite make sense of it. The first time she used her magic to travel back in time and save Chloe, she unknowingly Reached <i>way</i> beyond her grasp and released the Paradox, not knowing any better. The released Paradox created an abyssal incursion in the form of the storm, though it took time to get to Arcadia bay. Other stuff happens, Max saves Chloe some more, figures out how to contain the Paradox from her spells, (hence the nosebleeds and such), but eventually, the Abyssal entity in the form of the storm reaches Arcadia bay. Luckily (or perhaps unluckily) for Max, she has time travel powers. She can go back in time and stop herself from casting that first over-Reached spell, so the Paradox never gets released, and the Abyssal storm is never created. But, doing so will mean Chloe will die. That is the kind of decision Mages have the responsibility to make.<br /> <br /> Obviously, yes, the ending is a little contrived. In a more open-ended format like a tabletop RPG there would have been nothing stopping Max from back and warninf the people of the impending storm rather than stopping the storm from happening. But the format is limited, and the options presented create a significant moral dilemma. But, if we examine the other options realistically, are they really any better? How many people are going to believe Max about the storm? Are the lives of the people who don't want to take some teenager's word that they need to evacuate worth less than the life of one girl, just because she's personally important to the player character and they're not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011396-why-life-is-strange-is-false-premise-on-wisdom?p=1011623#post1011623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Silver Ladder are totally right and Wisdom <i>is</i> artificially created moral code entwine in universe by Exarchs to punish all opposition on to what <i>could</i> be done with Supernal Magic on world.</div> </div> </div> </div>The salt is real. Sorry, but I don't see this implication from interpreting Life is Strange as a Mage story at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T14:03:19-08:00","id":1011656,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't even do the Arcadian Storm as a Paradox, if I were port Life is Strange into Mage. I would make it a unique Mystery centered about abnormal Destiny of Chloe's family; a complex web of Fate and Destiny that doesn't obey normal rules; if prevented, it spreads like Immediate Nimbus, infecting the whole town. Or something.<br /> Again, it's less a story about time travelling, and more a story that uses time travel as a device to tell a tale of teenager-to-adult pains and transformations.<br /> <br /> edit<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011396-why-life-is-strange-is-false-premise-on-wisdom?p=1011623#post1011623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Or Silver Ladder are totally right and Wisdom <i>is</i> artificially created moral code entwine in universe by Exarchs to punish all opposition on to what <i>could</i> be done with Supernal Magic on world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wisdom is amoral. It's about understanding that when you do X, then Y happens. It's about insight, calculation, seeing bigger picture. You can be a Wise serial killer, and a really great Unwise person. In fact, most of popular protagonists would hover at low Wisdom, and many villains would be relatively high Wisdom (all the &quot;cold&quot; smart mastermind types, basically). <br /> <br /> Being Wise is not acting any way in particular. Is understanding what you do, why you do it, what will be the consequences and accepting responsibility for them. Nothing more, nothing less. If you are going to unleash mass murder with perfect clarity of your actions and without blinking an eye, then you are Wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 12-03-2016, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T15:56:20-08:00","id":1011708,"title":"","content":"Life is Strange - IMO, it was about a 14-year-old moving through the 5 stages of grief after seeing someone she may have not even known killed in the bathroom but in any event, let me run two scenarios by you for story seeds:<br /> <br /> 1) What if Max never left the bathroom? The entire game is her having a psychotic break after watching a total stranger shot and killed. She makes the entire story up as an escapism to deal with the harsh existential crisis that just slapped her in the face.<br /> <br /> If this is the take away from the game then it becomes a picture of an innocent dealing with denial and you could spin it into an innocence game as a 14-year-old is trying to cope with watching a girl get merc'd in the bathroom by diving deeper and deeper into her onerios and denying reality. If she fails to accept that Chloe is dead, she becomes a banisher or never awakens though if she accepts it she becomes either Mastigos or Acanthus.<br /> <br /> 2) Another inception style mind twist that's more Moros, what if Max is actually Rachael Ambers? She's been tossed into the dirt after having a bullet to the portion of brain that handles with cognitive self-awareness and the game we play is her Ego (Max) and her Id (Chloe) trying to solve the death of the personae (Rachael). The maelstrom then signals the brain death, while Max's powers are all part of the Rachael searching her own memories without the capacity to identify her Self. Chloe's death is the death of natural function which is why she nearly dies disaster after disaster an ounce of self-preservation the entire game.<br /> <br /> With this logic you could say that it\u2019s the awakening of either Moros or Masitgos. Another angle, you could say that Rachael is an incredibly powerful, gifted, or fated Mage and this event is a threshold seeking with her untimely demise being the end of a mystery play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6516-mefathiel8","name":"mefathiel8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T02:03:04-08:00","id":1011911,"title":"","content":"Really, the more and more I look at discussions about Integrity and its equivalents, I do wonder how many people still think they're playing the Unequivocally Good Guys Whose Every Heroic Act Is Morally Vindicated while playing a Chronicles of Darkness game.<br /> <br /> Most CoD games aren't about supernaturally gifted humans who sometimes commit monstrous acts, despite genuinely trying to do good and save the world. They're more likely to be about inhuman monsters who sometimes discover that there's still something human inside them that's worth holding onto, despite following their alien urges and compulsions.<br /> <br /> Granted, it's a case-by-case situation where every table differs in style, especially with a modular game system where people are expected to hack rules in any way that pleases them if that makes a better game for their table, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T02:26:20-08:00","id":1012458,"title":"","content":"Char, if you feel that this should go to different thread, could you extract this post, post I quote, and the post Axelgear was responding to and create something like &quot;Price of Magic&quot;? I'm talking about it here, because I feel Wyrds objection to Life is Strange is very relevant here, but I can see why it could fit it's own thread more. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011396-why-life-is-strange-is-false-premise-on-wisdom?p=1011618#post1011618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your powers having a terrible price isn't really one of Mage's themes, though. The idea that having control over Fate (and using said control) having innate negative consequences is something the setting seems to deliberately <i>not</i> have (or at least doesn't state up-front). The bad stuff that comes from monkeying with Fate and the horrible chains of unintended side-effects aren't because the gods decided to fuck you; they are <i>your </i>fault, absolutely and decidedly. If it's just an automatic thing that happens no matter what, it removes the whole idea of trying to balance Wisdom with action and instead makes it a question of total abstinence for any sane person or reckless abandon for everyone else.<br /> <br /> Mage gives you a really shiny, pretty rope and goodness, look at that, you've made it into a noose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but look at other Arcana.<br /> When you decide &quot;I want to get some zombies going&quot; in the morning, corpses don't pop up into existence from nowhere. You need to go dig some graves, kill some animals, buy them from shady sources, and so on; you are interacting with the world in questionable ways that might have consequences, intrude into private space of other people (like, who gave you right to animate dead bodies without consent of the previous occupant or their family?) and so on. Your zombies don't pop up conveniently into existence from nowhere; it's the same reason why people in DND 5 have problems with Necromancer Wizard archetype being core, as it's main function and gimmick is creating undead, which is problematic as *tons of characters find that practice to be wrong and evil*. <br /> Is it evil in Mage? No, but it can lead you to do &quot;evil&quot; things and trample over others in order to fulfill your selfish desire.<br /> Similar case with second major &quot;point of power&quot; of Death; Ghost manipulation. Ghosts allow you to do stuff, a lot of stuff, but you are treading on slippery ground here; do Ghosts deserve their own rights and right to be undisturbed? How do you (aside of mechanical Rank) differentate if this is a Rank 1/0 Ghost which is totally fine to rip apart for Mana whenever you feel thirsty, or if is it self aware enough that doing so would be monstrous cruelty? What gives you right to basically enslave and mind rape Ghosts to do your bidding? <br /> And third, well, Souls. Try poking at someone's Soul using Death and not be called a Left Handed prick. <br /> <br /> Mind is similar, as pretty much anything that isn't targeting you is controversial and potentially &quot;monstrous from the core&quot;; your Mind magic will probably leave behind broken people, people who got violated by your magic in worst ways possible even if you had great intentions. What is worse? Mind Controlling someone into telling you everything, or interrogating them and punching them few times? You can have a discussion here, a dilemma, and again, game provides you with tools to &quot;hang yourself&quot; without explicit &quot;GM is targeting me help there is nothing like this in the books&quot;.<br /> <br /> Spirit is probably the best example of &quot;giving you a tool&quot;, as you have a whole living, breathing ecosystem that *will* react to your manipulations, and your actions will have consequences. You have a whole subsystem to track these consequences and put them in motion; it\\s still very abstract, but if you change local resonance from &quot;Murderlicious&quot; to &quot;Vomit Inducing Sweet&quot;, you can only blame yourself for Murder Spirits going elsewhere to feed. It's logical and introduced into the game. For other Arcana, like Forces, you can extrapolate using &quot;real world rules&quot;; if you are fucking with electricity, it's easy to figure out you could cause unnecessary damage in local equipment. Playing with weather will unshape the weather patterns, and so on.<br /> <br /> Fate and Time are abstract enough that there is nothing really to extrapolate from, and they also don't have anything similar to &quot;Spirit World Economy&quot; to help you check how you are hanging yourself. System doesn't help you with telling a story about how you are cutting a good luck here and taping it with a Fatetape to that person here; it helps you tell stories about willing Event X into reality, without asking &quot;how do you do that?&quot;, &quot;who suffers because of that?&quot; and &quot;what are going to be consequences?&quot; <br /> There is never a reason to ask yourself if it's right to use your Fate/Time magic, because unlike other Arcana, there is no one hurt by your actions. All frills, no bitter pills. You want that guard to open the doors? Mind will literally violate him to do so; Spirit will violate a spirit to violate him to do it; Fate will just make it happen, because why not. <br /> For a path that talks all about consequences and interconnections, your magic is consequence-less and not connected to anything. It also lacks the tool to introduce these to the stories without it feeling like &quot;GM targeting&quot; and &quot;GM punishment&quot;. <br /> And then you have a situation like this thread, where &quot;consequences of your Magic&quot; are seen as unfair punishment when introduced into a story. While you can argue that &quot;a good GM will just introduce it and their players will just be happy with a good story&quot;, a lot of players will feel like it's undue punishment and gm dickery, because *there is nothing in the mechanics of the game that told them about their spells having those consequences.&quot; <br /> If I'm going to ever have patience to try fixing Fate, I would do something similar to Sympathy System, where you are targeting individual threads of Destiny and Fate, and if you want to make someone who is Lucky Unlucky, you need to either find an Unlucky person and steal it (like you steal Sympathy) or, if you are good enough (read, Fate 4), directly transform Luck into Unluck. And so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T20:22:20-08:00","id":1012957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011396-why-life-is-strange-is-false-premise-on-wisdom?p=1012458#post1012458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fate and Time are abstract enough that there is nothing really to extrapolate from, and they also don't have anything similar to &quot;Spirit World Economy&quot; to help you check how you are hanging yourself. System doesn't help you with telling a story about how you are cutting a good luck here and taping it with a Fatetape to that person here; it helps you tell stories about willing Event X into reality, without asking &quot;how do you do that?&quot;, &quot;who suffers because of that?&quot; and &quot;what are going to be consequences?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate gets you the desired result through whatever channels allow that result to come about fairly rapidly \u2014 the path of least resistance is not the path of fewest complications, which is part of why the Acanthus tap into archetypes that trend between flighty take-the-problems-as-they-come sorts and obsessive micromanagement fiends.<br /> <br /> A major point of half the &quot;some shit just happens&quot; spells in Fate is that you have no means of knowing what vectors a given adjustment will take. That's not something you can model with a system for an economy or ecology, because the sort of tracking that you'd need to keep up with the complex interactions that Fate spells mess with takes Time or a very wide net of inquiry. If your players think &quot;I'm going to take a gamble and have my desired outcome accomplished through whatever means are easiest with this spell&quot; having a ripple effect is unfair, pretty much nothing is going to convince them otherwise in a framework where magic exists in a populated setting full of moving parts that don't exist purely to facilitate the aims of their spellcasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T21:29:39-08:00","id":1012982,"title":"","content":"Well, duh.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">words</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T21:50:37-08:00","id":1012994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011396-why-life-is-strange-is-false-premise-on-wisdom?p=1011911#post1011911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, the more and more I look at discussions about Integrity and its equivalents, I do wonder how many people still think they're playing the Unequivocally Good Guys Whose Every Heroic Act Is Morally Vindicated while playing a Chronicles of Darkness game.<br /> <br /> Most CoD games aren't about supernaturally gifted humans who sometimes commit monstrous acts, despite genuinely trying to do good and save the world. They're more likely to be about inhuman monsters who sometimes discover that there's still something human inside them that's worth holding onto, despite following their alien urges and compulsions.<br /> <br /> Granted, it's a case-by-case situation where every table differs in style, especially with a modular game system where people are expected to hack rules in any way that pleases them if that makes a better game for their table, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it really hard to tell. On one hand, people aren't going to show up on the forums complaining that the game is working exactly as they expected it to, so discussions are <i>always</i> going to be biased, outside of Actual Plays. (And in my experience, most Actual Plays for Mage are pretty good about recognizing the PCs are not squeaky-clean whitehats.) On the other hand, I think that most people (including me) struggle with their own monstrosity and aren't 100% willing to engage with it to the degree that makes CofD stories so good.<br /> <br /> On the gripping hand, wyrdhamster is a regular user who makes threads about how a particular movie or TV show has specific mappings to random Mage bits on a relatively frequent basis. Sturgeon's Law applies just from the sheer volume of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T23:32:43-08:00","id":1013030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011396-why-life-is-strange-is-false-premise-on-wisdom?p=1012994#post1012994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the gripping hand, wyrdhamster is a regular user who makes threads about how a particular movie or TV show has specific mappings to random Mage bits on a relatively frequent basis. Sturgeon's Law applies just from the sheer volume of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I come from paradigm where better is to talk about bits and pieces of game from various media. As we do not have, for example, official <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> video game - we must take inspirations from other places. And discussion on those is also enlightening, even pointing to place where they <i>not work</i> as MtAw inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T23:53:08-08:00","id":1013038,"title":"","content":"The problem is that Life is Strange is written from such a non-Acanthusian attitude that's hard to parallel it or comment on it through those lens on this particular point.<br /> <br /> Now, being perfectly clear, I think the ending is bullshit, a sore strike against an otherwise beautiful game. But If I have to interpret the game through the lens of Awakening, it's not an Acanthus story, but a <i>Moros</i> story. It's a game about transformation and transition (only by virtue of that fucking ending, but still those things none the less) where in Max's desire for permanence is fundamentally shown to be a Lie-that life is fleeting and that eternity is a lie. Throughout the story, Max is trying to just sort of keep things together and to return her world to the way it was as a kid, and even improve upon it with her choices. Now, her choices <i>do</i> change things-this is <i>the</i> reason the ending pisses me off, because it strips away all of that-but if you pay attention to the major beats, even before then, pretty much there's a limit based on the details, and the ending wipes away all illusion of meaning in the grand scheme of things. In the end, regardless of how you have to go, Max's story is about how you have to let go of <i>something</i>, because the world just keeps changing, and to cling one way or another just means the loss of everything-and really, the world will move on without the small town of Arcadia Bay, without Chloe-without Max.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. LiS is a terrible Acanthus story because of it's end, but it's a great Moros-with-Time story. The biggest problem is that up to that fucking god damned ending, it played out <i>like</i> an Acanthus story.<br /> <br /> But then again, Life is Strange is not an Awakening story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-14-2018, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T00:19:16-08:00","id":1013049,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was just being generally miffed about Integrity, rather than translating various media into CofD and/or specifically aiming ofr wyrd.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, a Moros Awakening, Arc says... now that's an intriguing angle to look at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T01:49:49-08:00","id":1013070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011396-why-life-is-strange-is-false-premise-on-wisdom?p=1013038#post1013038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, yeah. LiS is a terrible Acanthus story because of it's end, but it's a great Moros-with-Time story. The biggest problem is that up to that fucking god damned ending, it played out <i>like</i> an Acanthus story.<br /> <br /> But then again, Life is Strange is not an Awakening story.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's great and simple answer, even if Acanthi in me weeps in this turn out... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T19:58:20-08:00","id":1013554,"title":"","content":"I feel it worth noting that the Acanthusian attitude about Always A Third Option must be noted not as Wisdom, but as Hubris. Not in all situations, mind you-there are times when the constraints of choices are basically the Lie. But then there are also times where the Third Option is in defiance of Consequences, where obsession with vision overrides one's will-in-harmony-with-Truth(ie, being a Wise mage means not everything is about You and What You Want, mage).<br /> <br /> There times to defy the odds, and then there are times to let it roll. The Acanthus are bad at the latter, the Moros are bad at the former. Awakening is not an abandonment of the Lie, it's just rising above one layer of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}